 7871:                                 ; idle_fuel_learn
 7872:                                 ;   analysis [high]: OBD1 CALC_DRAGTORQUE: after CAL_DRAG_ADAPT_MINRUNTM, with stable idle target, RPM within
 7873:                                 ;        +/-CAL_DRAG_ADAPT_MAXRPMERR, PTO off and pedal 0, it learns idle fuel (drag torque) into one of 4 cells:
 7874:                                 ;        P/N or drive-stationary-with-brake, each A/C on/off (MUX9 >= $56). Otherwise it picks the active cell
 7875:                                 ;        into DRAGTQ_ADJUST clamped to CAL_DRAG_ADAPT_MIN/MAX_ADJ, and computes the roughness/RPM-sag idle fuel a
 7876:                                 ;   OBD1 CALC_DRAGTORQUE (match 1.00 p1-exact): done in 50ms job - looks like part of engine governing... base
 7877:                                 ;        torque or something???
 7878:                                 ;   called from: run_50ms_job
