14624:                                 ; calc_shift_ratio_profile_BA38
14625:                                 ;   analysis [medium]: State machine for the commanded gear ratio $1889 during a shift. The state bits are in
14626:                                 ;        $6C/$6D/$6E and are reset by sub_BD07. Each state is driven by shift-phase bits $1B46.1/.2, $77 and
14627:                                 ;        $85.4. $188C is a tick timer. The state picks a start ratio $1894 and a target ratio $1892
14628:                                 ;        (tbl_386B/386D/386F/3869 via sub_BD0F) plus a delay ($188F) and ramp length ($188B, from
14629:                                 ;        tbl_3876/tbl_3873/$1B64). It then
14630:                                 ;   called from: Central_Scheduler
