22915:                                 ; sub_F40E
22916:                                 ;   analysis [low]: Sets 008E.4/clears 0091.5 once engine runs or vehicle moves. Then for the anti-theft message
22917:                                 ;        (sub_703D index $20, if 200D.1) and two external-module messages (indexes $22/$26, if 200D.4) it updates
22918:                                 ;        the receive status (1DE1/1DD6/1DDC) and timeout counters (1DE2/1DD7/1DDD, limit 50). A status of $FF
22919:                                 ;        means the message is lost. Skipped while FLAGS0.2 (ignition-off) is set.
22920:                                 ;   called from: run_100ms_engine_tasks_EC95
